OCGRAPH 1
# A THING THAT REACTS TO BEING HIT, and remembers how often. Still no C# anywhere in this project.
#
# Two capabilities meet here. ENTRY OnHit has existed since 75be56b, but until 6d7ff99 nothing could
# SEND one from a graph -- GraphHost.Fire was reachable only from C#, so a graph could declare a
# reaction it had no way of ever receiving. And VAR (a45e32f) is what lets the count survive the
# tick, stored per GraphHost instance, so two targets placed from this one file keep separate scores
# rather than sharing one.
NAME Target
DESCRIPTION Counts the hits it receives. One file, any number of instances, independent counts.

CLASS AN_Target Actor

PARAM entity int

# FLOAT, not int, and the engine told me why: Add takes float pins and there is no integer
# Add in the palette, so an int VAR wired into one fails at load with
#   "Link prev.value (Int) to next.a (Float): type mismatch"
# -- a good error, caught before anything ran rather than counting wrongly at runtime.
VAR hits float 0

# ---- the reaction --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An ENTRY is not a node type: it names which node begins a chain, and OnHit differs from OnStart and
# OnTick only in that nobody calls it for you. A host -- or, since 6d7ff99, another graph's FireEvent
# -- has to fire it by name.
ENTRY hit OnHit
NODE hit OnHit

NODE one ConstFloat
PIN one value out float 1.0

NODE prev GetVar var=hits
NODE next Add
LINK prev.value next.a
LINK one.value next.b

NODE store SetVar var=hits
LINK hit.exec store.exec
LINK next.result store.value

# ---- reporting -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A SEPARATE GetVar, deliberately not the `prev` node above. An OUT record pulls a pure data
# expression, and pulling `prev` would report the count as it was BEFORE this hit was stored -- an
# off-by-one that looks like a lost hit. Reading through its own node after the write is the honest
# shape, and the same trap caught a reviewer building acceptance evidence for this very feature.
ENTRY tick OnTick
NODE tick OnTick
NODE report GetVar var=hits

OUT report value
